<!--
  Server settings UTMStack depends on, pinned rather than inherited.

  date_time_input_format decides whether a timestamp written as RFC3339 — with
  the T separator and a Z, which is what the pipeline produces — is accepted.
  Its default is not stable across ClickHouse releases: 25.3 ships "basic",
  which rejects those outright, and later versions ship "best_effort", which
  accepts them. Relying on the default means an insert that works on one
  version fails on another, and the failure is per-row at write time.

  The server version is pinned to 25.8 for a related reason: 25.3 cannot parse
  a nested object into a JSON column through JSONEachRow at all, which is how
  every log and alert is written.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <profiles>
        <default>
            <date_time_input_format>best_effort</date_time_input_format>
        </default>
    </profiles>
</clickhouse>
